    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0312" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123M272/67a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-12T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 12,
                                1920, 2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Magruder has been ordered to assume the duties of Chargé d’Affaires <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ad interim</hi> at Helsingfors until the arrival of a
                    Minister. A letter accrediting him to Minister for Foreign Affairs is being
                    mailed to Madrid.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d166-f1"/> He should remain in Madrid
                    until Caffery has become familiar with the Embassy, but not later than February
                        10.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d166-f2"/> Request him to notify Department by
                    cable concerning the clerical and stenographic force which he will require for
                    the establishment of the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d166-f1" n="11" xml:id="d166-f1-content">
                <p>No file copy has been found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d166-f2" n="12" xml:id="d166-f2-content">
                <p>In a telegram of Jan. 27, the Ambassador reported: “Magruder left for London last
                    night <hi rendition="#italic">en-route</hi> to Helsingfors. He will report at
                    Embassy London for possible instructions.” In a telegram of Feb. 17, addressed
                    to Magruder at London, he was directed to “proceed Stockholm and await further
                    instructions.” (File Nos. 123M272/71, 75.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
